  "track.cleancode.cap.fits": "Code on the left loads into working memory; the new requirement below edits the code; the reminder is on the right. When working memory turns red, the reader is holding more than 7 things.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.long.s1.title": "Read lines 1–6: input checks",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.long.s1.explain": "Three ifs, five variables: req, doctors, doctor, slot, clock. Still fits in your head.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.ev.long.s1": "Read lines 1–6: input checks",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.long.s2.title": "Read lines 7–13: the fee",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.long.s2.explain": "Three more ifs and a for: 8 paths. Add fee, vouchers, code, v: 9 variables. Both are past 7 and the function is only two-thirds done.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.ev.long.s2": "Read lines 7–13: the fee",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.long.s3.title": "Read lines 14–18: save and remind",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.long.s3.explain": "One more if: 9 paths; add booking, repo, hours, reminders: 13 variables. The function is only 19 lines, under the 24-line threshold, so counting lines misses the problem.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.ev.long.s3": "Read lines 14–18: save and remind",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.long.s4.title": "New requirement: a 0 fee saves and returns at once",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.long.s4.explain": "The editor looks only at the fee part and inserts an if with an early return after the for loop. Every free booking now skips line 21: nobody gets a reminder.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.ev.long.s4": "New requirement: a 0 fee saves and returns at once",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.split.s1.title": "Read bookAppointment: six lines, top-down",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.split.s1.explain": "One if, six variables. Each line is a step at the same level of abstraction: check, compute the fee, save, remind.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.ev.split.s1": "Read bookAppointment: six lines, top-down",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.split.s2.title": "Read validate when you need the details",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.split.s2.explain": "Two ifs, three variables. Reading it does not require remembering the fee or the reminder.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.ev.split.s2": "Read validate when you need the details",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.split.s3.title": "Read feeFor",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.split.s3.explain": "Two ifs, four variables. The voucher loop lives in vouchers.totalFor: the complexity does not vanish, it moves elsewhere.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.ev.split.s3": "Read feeFor",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.split.s4.title": "The same requirement, edited in feeFor",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.s.split.s4.explain": "The fee never goes below zero: coerceAtLeast(0) on line 21. bookAppointment is unchanged, and the reminder line still runs for every booking.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.ev.split.s4": "The same requirement, edited in feeFor",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.co.try": "Walk four steps; each reads one more part of the code. Watch the two rows of slots: paths and variables.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.co.long.s2": "Seemann (ch.7): agree on a threshold and watch it; past 7, decompose before adding a new branch. The 7 is symbolic; what works is having a threshold. [[src:book-seemann]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.co.long.s3": "Seemann (ch.7): he gets uncomfortable when a C# method nears 20 lines and picks 24 as an arbitrary threshold (the 80 × 24 VT100 screen). Line count is one view; this function passes the line threshold but not the path threshold. [[src:book-seemann]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.co.long.s4": "An early return in the middle of a long function skips everything after it. The editor was not careless: what came after was outside what their head could hold at that moment.",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.co.split.s1": "Martin (Clean Code ch.3): every statement in a function should sit at one level of abstraction, and code should read top-down like a narrative, each function followed by those one level below (the stepdown rule). [[src:book-cleancode]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.co.split.s2": "Seemann (7.2.7): count local variables, parameters and class fields. validate uses req, clock and doctors: three things. [[src:book-seemann]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.co.split.s3": "Seemann (A.8): cyclomatic complexity is also the minimum number of tests to cover every path of a function. feeFor has 3 paths, so it needs at least 3 tests. [[src:book-seemann]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.fits.co.split.s4": "The change lands in exactly one small function. Whatever lives outside it does not need to be held in your head, so it cannot be skipped by accident.",
  "track.cleancode.vz.tab.fits": "Working memory",
  "track.cleancode.vz.fits.cap": "Function being read: {fn}. Each slot is one thing the reader must hold in their head; the row of 7 slots is Seemann's threshold, the red row below is what goes beyond it.",
